         <dc:description>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Percentiles of Price-Earnings Ratios for All U.S.Traded Firms with Market Capitalization Over $200 Million, 1963â€“2010. P/E ratios were relatively low in the 1970s and high in the 1960s and 1990s. The median is typically above 10.0. (The figure covers firms with positive&#xA;earnings only.)</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:description>
         <dc:subject>
            <rdf:Bag>
               <rdf:li>Keep blank</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Bag>
         </dc:subject>
      </rdf:Description>
